From 290e4c50b4c39643a750771d0066c2ede3aa52aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:39:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Flatpacks: the workbench does something now

84 flatpacks across 15 families on 15 shared models, re-encoded out of the
rev240 cache. Work-at on any of the five workbench tiers opens a family grid,
then that family's ladder, and makes a flatpack that can be spent at the
matching hotspot in place of the planks.

The xp is paid on assembly, not on making - which is what makes a flatpack
worth having in OSRS, and the only thing stopping one set of planks paying
twice. A held flatpack is preferred over held materials and the message says
which was spent.

The set was found in the cache, not from memory: a flatpack is named exactly
like the piece it builds, and the only thing separating the 91 of them from
every other obj is the examine "How does it all fit in there?".

Also fixes a checker that could not go red. Group 38 of poh_battery runs
genfurn.py in place and restores any generated file the re-run changed - but
poh_flatpacks.obj and obj.pack were not in that list, so group 38 quietly
regenerated a deliberate break away and every later group read a repaired
tree. A generated file missing from that list is not checked by anything.

rs2check 0 ERROR / 0 CHECK; poh_battery ALL PASS (52 groups);
poh_mutate 47/47 caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J1qUhTcu63bJ3hCBBxy7nU
